UID:35f7402c4b434042@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261027T175726Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] State of Maine v. Devon M. Stewart
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT Reporter of Decisions \nDecision:
   2026 ME 104 \nDocket: Som-25-305 \nArgued: March 5\, 2026 \nDecided:  Oc
 tober 27\, 2026 \n \nPanel:  STANFILL\, C.J.\, and MEAD\, CONNORS\, LAWREN
 CE\, DOUGLAS\, and LIPEZ\, JJ.  \n \n \nSTATE OF MAINE \n \nv. \n \nDEVON 
 M. STEWART \n \n \nLAWRENCE\, J. \n[¶1]  Devon M. Stewart appeals from a 
 judgment of conviction of one \ncount of gross sexual assault  entered by 
 the trial court (Somerset County\, \nMullen\, C.J.) after a jury trial.  S
 tewart challenges the sufficiency of the evidence\, \nargues that the tria
 l court erred by admitting in evidence the victim’s 9-1-1 call \nand her
  testimony regarding Stewart’s out-of-court statement\, and asserts that
  \nthe trial court abused its discretion  during the second step of the se
 ntencing \nanalysis by improperly setting his probation for longer than  w
 hat is allowed \nunder 17-A M.R.S. § 1804(1)(A) (2025).1  We conclude tha
 t there was sufficient \nevidence to support a conviction of gross sexual 
 assault by compulsion\, that \n \n1  Title 17-A M.R.S. § 1804(1) has sinc
 e been amended but not in any way that affects this appeal.  \nSee P.L. 20
 25\, ch. 207\, § 2 (effective Sep. 24\, 2025) (codified at 17-A M.R.S. §
  1804(1) (2026)). \n 2 \nStewart waived his argument regarding the 9 -1-1 
 call\, and that the trial court \ndid not err in admitti ng the victim’s
  testimony regarding Stewart’s statement.  \nHowever\, we also conclude 
 that the trial court erred by improperly sentencing \nStewart to a longer 
 probationary period than is allowed by statute. 2  We \ntherefore affirm t
 he conviction but vacate the sentence and remand for \nresentencing. \nI. 
  BACKGROUND \n[¶2]  Viewing the evidence in the light most favorable to t
 he verdict\, the \njury rationally could have found the following facts be
 yond a reasonable doubt.  \nSee State v. Hansen\, 2020 ME 43\, ¶ 2\, 228 
 A.3d 1082. \n [¶3]  On February 17\, 2023\, the sixteen -year-old victim 
 was walking in \nWaterville toward Fairfield.  The victim recognized Stewa
 rt\, a former \nschoolmat\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcour
 t/2026/26me104.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me104.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
